The changes below are what a G1 sim2sim loop needs: driving the real controller
binary — the one in ../deploy — against a simulated robot, unattended.

Changes
-------

ADDED
  unitree_robots/g1/g1_29dof_mjlabdyn.xml
      Per-joint armature = actuator reflected inertia, damping and frictionloss
      zeroed, matching the plant mjlab trains against. The stock file's uniform
      armature 0.01 / damping 0.05 / frictionloss 0.2 is a different robot.
  unitree_robots/g1/scene_29dof_mjlabdyn.xml
      Flat scene around the above; the new default. White studio theme (white
      sky, white floor with black checker edges, no reflectance) so a recording
      is legible. Upstream's own scenes are untouched.
  unitree_robots/g1/scene_obstacles.xml
      A slalom corridor — somewhere to actually steer a joystick policy.
  simulate/src/lcm_joystick.{h,cc}
      joystick_type: "lcm" — the pad arrives as joy_t over LCM rather than from
      /dev/input, so an unattended run can publish the chords the FSM needs.
  simulate/lcm_types/smp_hw_lcm.lcm
      The joy_t definition, identical to ../lcm_types/smp_hw_lcm.lcm's copy of
      it. Bindings are generated at build time, never committed.
  simulate/cyclonedds.xml
      Loopback DDS config, so the simulator and the controller can find each
      other on one machine.

MODIFIED
  simulate/CMakeLists.txt
      MuJoCo located by search (-DMUJOCO_DIR, $MUJOCO_DIR, the gitignored
      mujoco/ symlink, ~/.mujoco, /opt) instead of requiring the symlink.
  simulate/src/main.cc
      Headless mode: a physics loop with no window, for a machine with no
      display or an X display without GLX. The elastic band releases on a timer
      there, since there is no key to press. Side panels default off.
  simulate/src/param.h
      headless, band_release_s, show_left_ui, show_right_ui,
      joystick_lcm_channel, joystick_lcm_url, and the flags --headless /
      --band-release / --ui / --joystick. The last one makes the gamepad source
      selectable at launch instead of only in config.yaml, so one config serves
      both a hand-driven run and a scripted one.
  simulate/src/unitree_sdk2_bridge.h
      Dispatches joystick_type: "lcm".
  simulate/config.yaml
      Defaults for the G1 loop, and the DDS interface agreement that is
      otherwise a silent "waiting for rt/lowstate" hang.

REMOVED when vendoring
  unitree_robots/{a2,b2,b2w,go2,go2w,h1,h1_2,r1}
      249 MB of meshes for robots this repository has no use for. Pull them
      from upstream if you need one.
  example/
      Per-robot SDK examples, none of them G1 policy work.
